• To concentrate our available resources on the fields with the higher threat, we reassign one drone (Drone_1 originally protecting Field_3) from Field_3 to join Field_1. This gives Field_1 full protection with 4 drones.
• That leaves Drone_4 (the remaining drone originally protecting Field_3) not needed for full protection (and switching it would only yield a partial, and thus not very effective, defense for Field_2 or Field_3). So we assign it to idle.
• In this way we fully protect the high‐threat fields (Field_4 and Field_1) while leaving the lower‐threat fields (Field_2 and Field_3) unprotected.
This assignment aims to minimize overall field damage as described.
